-- Q1. What is a trigger in PL/SQL?
-- Ans: Trigger ek stored PL/SQL block hai jo kisi
-- specified database event par automatically execute hota hai.

-- Q2. What is the purpose of EMP_AUDIT?
-- Ans: EMP_AUDIT table mein naye employee ki details
-- aur insertion date store hoti hai.

-- Q3. What is TRG_EMP_INSERT?
-- Ans: Ye trigger ka naam hai.

-- Q4. What does AFTER INSERT mean?
-- Ans: Employee record insert hone ke baad trigger execute hota hai.

-- Q5. What is FOR EACH ROW?
-- Ans: Iska matlab trigger har affected row ke liye
-- alag se execute hoga.

-- Q6. What is :NEW?
-- Ans: :NEW trigger mein insert ya update hone wali
-- row ki new values access karne ke liye use hota hai.

-- Q7. What is SYSDATE?
-- Ans: SYSDATE database server ki current date aur time return karta hai.

-- Q8. Does a trigger need to be called manually?
-- Ans: Nahi, trigger specified event hone par automatically execute hota hai.

-- Q9. What happens if a new employee is inserted?
-- Ans: Employee ki details automatically EMP_AUDIT mein store hoti hain.

-- Q10. What is the purpose of SHOW ERRORS?
-- Ans: Isse trigger compile karte waqt aayi errors check kar sakte hain.

-- Q11. What is the difference between BEFORE and AFTER triggers?
-- Ans: BEFORE trigger event se pehle execute hota hai,
-- jabki AFTER trigger event ke baad execute hota hai.

-- Q12. Why is COMMIT used?
-- Ans: COMMIT transaction ke changes permanently save karta hai.

-- Q13. Can one table have multiple triggers?
-- Ans: Haan, ek table par different events aur conditions
-- ke liye multiple triggers ho sakte hain.

-- Q14. What does :NEW.EID represent?
-- Ans: Ye insert hone wali employee row ki EID value represent karta hai.

-- Q15. What is an audit table?
-- Ans: Audit table database mein important changes ya
-- activities ka record maintain karti hai.
